    "lawCode": "Add §630-m, Tax L; add §99-ss, St Fin L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S1185\n\nSPONSOR: ADDABBO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the tax law and the state finance law, in relation to\ngifts for the support of congressional chartered veterans service organ-\nizations\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo create a voluntary contribution on the state personal income tax\nreturn for congressional chartered veterans service organizations.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 adds section 630-i to the tax law, which creates the option to\ncontribute to the congressional chartered veterans service organizations\nfund in New York State personal income tax returns.\n\nSection 2 adds section 99-ii to the state finance law, which creates the\nVeterans Service Organizations Fund.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nVeterans are entitled to certain services. Accessing these services can\nbe difficult, though. Congressional chartered Veterans' service organ-\nizations help cut through the red tape and connect veterans with the\nservices that they have earned.. By allowing taxpayers to voluntarily\ncontribute to the Veterans Service Organizations Fund, we are providing\nbudget-neutral support to our veterans.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2019: S. 2740A - Passed Senate.\n\n2020: S. 2740A - Referred to Veterans, Homeland Security and Military\nAffairs.\n\n2021-22: S. 4069A - Passed Senate.\n\n2023-24: S.2019 - Passed Senate.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n",
